 Nuclear reaction model code EMPIRE-3.2.3 Malta                   3925 1451
 (SVN rev. 4867 )                                                 3925 1451
 by M.W.Herman et al [EMP,EMP-man].                               3925 1451
                                                                  3925 1451
 EMPIRE dimensions (dimension.h):                                 3925 1451
  NDNUC= 150  NDEXCLUS= 20  NDEX= 201  NDLW= 100                  3925 1451
  LEVCC= 40  NDLV= 40  NDBR= 40  NDMSCS= 4                        3925 1451
                                                                  3925 1451
 CROSS-SECTION EVALUATION PROCEDURE                               3925 1451
                                                                  3925 1451
 Adopted procedure is based on careful theoretical                3925 1451
 analysis utilizing available experimental data and               3925 1451
 nuclear reaction model calculations.                             3925 1451
                                                                  3925 1451
 This code integrates into a single system a number               3925 1451
 of important modules and features:                               3925 1451
                                                                  3925 1451
 - Spherical and deformed Optical Model including                 3925 1451
   coupled-channels code ECIS06 by J. Raynal                      3925 1451
 - Soft-rotator deformed Optical Model including                  3925 1451
   coupled-channels code OPTMAN by E.Soukhovitskii                3925 1451
   and coworkers                                                  3925 1451
 - Hauser-Feshbach statistical model including                    3925 1451
   width fluctuation correction, and the                          3925 1451
   optical model for fission with partial damping                 3925 1451
 - Quantum-mechanical MSD TUL model (codes ORION &                3925 1451
   TRISTAN by H.Lenske), and MSC NVWY model                       3925 1451
 - Exciton model with Iwamoto-Harada cluster                      3925 1451
   emission and Kalbach systematic angular distr.                 3925 1451
   (code PCROSS by R.Capote et al)                                3925 1451
 - Hybrid Monte Carlo preequilibrium model(M.Blann)               3925 1451
   (code DDHMS by M.Chadwick, mod. by B.V.Carlson)                3925 1451
 - Complete gamma-ray cascade after emission of                   3925 1451
   each particle, including realistic treatment of                3925 1451
   discrete transitions                                           3925 1451
 - Access to OM segment of the RIPL library [RIPL]                3925 1451
 - Built-in input parameter files, such as masses,                3925 1451
   level density, discrete levels, fission barriers               3925 1451
   and gamma strength functions based on the RIPL                 3925 1451
   library [RIPL]                                                 3925 1451
 - Automatic retrieval of experimental data from the              3925 1451
   EXFOR library                                                  3925 1451
 - ENDF-6 formatting (code EMPEND by A.Trkov)                     3925 1451
   coupled to graphical presentation capabilities                 3925 1451
   (code ZVView by V. Zerkin) through the chain of                3925 1451
   PrePro codes by D. Cullen                                      3925 1451
 - ENDF checking codes (CHECKR, FIZCON, PSYCHE)                   3925 1451
 - Highly automated fitting of optical model                      3925 1451
   parameters (by B.V. Carlson)                                   3925 1451
 - KALMAN code for fitting experimental data and                  3925 1451
 - generating covariances                                         3925 1451
 - Support for NJOY                                               3925 1451
                                                                  3925 1451
                                                                  3925 1451
 PARAMETERIZATIONS                                                3925 1451
                                                                  3925 1451
 Following models and parameters were used in the                 3925 1451
 current evaluation:                                              3925 1451
                                                                  3925 1451
 Discrete levels were taken from the RIPL-3+                      3925 1451
 library based on the 2015 version of ENSDF.                      3925 1451
 ENDF formatting enabled                                          3925 1451
 Exclusive emission from CN and target enabled                    3925 1451
 Exclusive spectra available for residues distant                 3925 1451
   from CN up to 3 neut. or 3 prot.                               3925 1451
 GSM level densities (Ignatyuk)                                   3925 1451
 GDR first hump energy in  89Y  set to 15.40                      3925 1451
 GDR first hump width in  89Y  set to  3.10                       3925 1451
 GDR first hump cross section in  89Y  set to   64.00             3925 1451
 GDR second hump energy in  89Y  set to 17.05                     3925 1451
 GDR second hump width in  89Y  set to  3.00                      3925 1451
 GDR second hump cross section in  89Y  set to  189.00            3925 1451
 Quasideuteron photoabsorption cross section normalized by a facto3925 1451
 CN decay and Direct cross sections added incoherently            3925 1451
 CN angular distribution assumed isotropic                        3925 1451
 Traditional Hauser-Feschbach Tlj_{CC}(E)=Tlj_{GS}(E-Egs)         3925 1451
 E1 strength function set to RIPL SMLO                            3925 1451
 GDR parameters from RIPL/MLO-exp.data+Plujko systematics         3925 1451
 Gamma-transition multipolarity set to    2                       3925 1451
